  - S&P 500
abstract: >-
  Code, data pipeline, experiment ledger and manuscript for a study of whether
  a persistence state built from rolling long-memory estimates of range-based
  variance forecasts stock volatility beyond implied volatility, on 115
  S&P 500 stocks from November 2001 to April 2026. The state adds nothing to
  HAR-X (HAR plus VIX and MOVE) under any registered design; it is a
  window-inclusion indicator of the largest recent volatility episode, whose
  turning points move one-for-one with the estimation window. Includes
  point-in-time forecasting, panel Diebold-Mariano, Clark-West and
  Giacomini-White tests, an information-timing comparison, and
  volatility-managed portfolio evaluation.
